# Supabase
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key
SUPABASE_SERVICE_KEY=your-service-key

# Passwordless auth setup is configured in Supabase, not with client SMTP keys:
# - Configure/test production SMTP and email rate limits before relying on it.
# - Confirm signup AND Magic link templates must include a link and {{ .Token }}.
# - Allow /auth/callback redirects (including the next query string).
# - Keep Confirm email enabled; disabling it does not bypass email-code login.
# See docs/authentication.md for the dual link/code template and rollout checks.

# App
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=http://localhost:3000

# Merge engine (spec §3). On by default since step 6 of the markdown-canonical
# migration: document saves go through `propose -> merge`, which is what writes
# `body_md` and records a revision. Set to 0 to fall back to direct writes —
# a rollback lever, not a supported mode (saves stop producing revisions).
# AQLI_MERGE_ENGINE=1

# OpenAI (required for embeddings + agent context retrieval)
OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...

# Linear (optional — enables issue/project preview in the doc sidebar)
LINEAR_API_KEY=lin_api_...

# GitHub needs no keys here. A workspace admin pastes a personal access token
# (scopes: repo, admin:repo_hook) in Settings → Integrations, and it is stored
# per workspace. The webhook secret is generated per connection.
#
# This is what dropping Composio bought a self-hoster: one fewer account to
# create and three fewer environment variables. For reference, they were:
#   COMPOSIO_API_KEY, COMPOSIO_WEBHOOK_SECRET, COMPOSIO_WEBHOOK_URL
